{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1554815061,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MzA5NTU5MjI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3306","origin":"github"},"title":"testrepo setup does not protect dotfiles against git-annex","message":"Older tests tend to use testrepo as if they were DataLad datasets. However, I keep forgetting that they are not, as they are generated without DataLad tooling and make no attempt to even look like actual datasets. Symptoms:\n\n1. They do not have a dataset ID\n2. They do not carry the default gitattriutes\n    ```\n    * annex.backend=MD5E\n    **/.git* annex.largefiles=nothing\n    ``` \n\nNow one could argue whether this is a bug or a feature, but in the concrete case of adding a subdataset to a non-dataset, `.gitmodules` ends up being annexed -- which is a problem.\nGitRepo.add_submodule() is not committing this change so various places need a fix, but I am not yet sure which approach is best.\n\nA symptom of this problem as the failing tests in                      https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3304: e.g. https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/jobs/517362633#L1781","files":null}]}